# Inlining SQL results
You can *inline* text content similar to JSX. In JSX, we could print a dynamic greeting like so:

```jsx
<span>Hello {username}</span>
```

You can tell `squid` to output inline text using scalar SQL braces in a similar fashion like so:

```md
Hello **{SELECT username FROM users WHERE age > 21}**!
```

This outputs:

Hello **{SELECT username FROM users WHERE age > 21}**!

Your query must select exactly *1 column* and *1 row*. If you try to select more than 1 column or 1 row:

```md
Hello **{SELECT user_id, username, age FROM users WHERE age > 20}**!
Hello **{SELECT username FROM users WHERE age > 20}**!
Hello **{SELECT user_id, username, age FROM users WHERE age > 20}**!
```

Then `squid` will throw an error.

If you want to format multiple values inline as plain-text, then use an aggregate like `GROUP_CONCAT()`:

```md
Hello {SELECT GROUP_CONCAT('**' || username || '**', ', ') FROM users;}!
```

Hello {SELECT GROUP_CONCAT('**' || username || '**', ', ') FROM users;}!
